add('connector', 'CrossClaim', f"""Separability check before data lands: read {PR} `== Separability`. From bytes, list every C1 item (in {C1I}) whose argv or files reach a file C2 will change (tools/souji-census.sh, tools/souji-evidence-cache.py, tools/souji-round9-selftest.sh via souji-verify/vault-verify/quarantine, r15 fixtures) — e.g. K07 via r17-census-hygiene, K08 via r17-jj-receipts --tool-dir tools, K03 via souji-quarantine.sh. For each, predict whether a Q71-only repair can move the item's output and how the counters would show it. Also: can a C1 restatement row move any C2 leg (does any G-guard read SCORECARD.md)? Deliver {D('cross-claim.md')}.""")
add('connector', 'RecurrenceScan', f"""Mistake-class recurrence scan: read the `## Mistakes`, `## Routed defects` and Step-1 defect lists in {L}/corpus/lessons/round-28*.md through round-32*.md (lessons and verifier spot-checks) and list each class with its round(s). Then read {PR}, {C1C}, {C2C}, {C1I}, {C2L} and say which classes this round's frozen design is exposed to (e.g. citing a wave path before its capture lands; a gate reading reported without a committed run; a frozen anchor that moves with lane content; a predicate a constants fixture meets) and which design element closes or fails to close each. Deliver {D('recurrence.md')}.""")
add('reviewer', 'PreregReview', f"""Review the frozen preregistration {PR} against the counters' code ({C1C}, {C2C}) and item files ({C1I}, {C2L}): (1) is the predicate the same sentence in the plan, the same condition in the code (exit 0 iff ...) and the same label in a receipt (§9 of the round prompt: plan, counter, receipt agree)? (2) do the kill rules and 'landing commit' definitions leave any reading unjudged? (3) does every Q70 leg exist in {FEAS} (feasibility leg per item shape; three stable base runs; anchor perturbation)? (4) are the do-nothing control and a junk control actually below target under the frozen code (re-run the C1 do-nothing at {PRE} in scratch {S('PreregReview')})? Findings with file:line.""")
add('scribe', 'DraftSkillRows', f"""Draft, as {D('skill-rows.md')}, (a) two SKILL.md `## Gate registry` rows in the exact column shape of the existing rows (read `git -C {L} show {PRE}:SKILL.md`, section `## Gate registry`) for `census/round-33/c1-counter.py` (capability-table currency) and `census/round-33/c2-counter.py`, with exit codes from their docstrings; (b) one SKILL error-pattern bullet for the trailing-slash TMPDIR class (string `case` patterns vs the kernel's single-slash readlink path), citing the SOURCES ids S224 (POSIX pathname resolution) and S225 (proc_pid_fd(5)) that wave scribes are opening; (c) one QUALITY.md criterion row draft (next free id after the last `| Q` row) for capability-table currency: a capability row's stated outcome is re-run at the round tip, and a drifted row is restated append-only with an executed cause commit — citing corpus/lessons/round-33.md. Mark every value you did not read from bytes `<L1>`.""")
add('simplifier', 'SpecHygieneW1', f"""Validate this wave's spec hygiene: read {L}/.ufo/waves/round-33/make-spec-w1.py and the rendered {L}/.ufo/waves/round-33/w1-dispatch.json. Check: distinct ids and prompts; roles only from the allowed 10; flash share (executor, scribe, critic, sentinel, revenger, simplifier) >= 50 %; attack share (reviewer, critic, mutation-tester) >= 25 %; every path absolute; every scratch path under {SCR}/<item>/; every delivery file under {W}/ and unique; no two executors told to change the same lane file; every item names what it builds or attacks. Report defects with item ids.""")

c = collections.Counter(i['role'] for i in ITEMS)
n = len(ITEMS)
assert len({i['item'] for i in ITEMS}) == n and len({i['prompt'] for i in ITEMS}) == n
flash = sum(c[r] for r in ('executor', 'scribe', 'critic', 'sentinel', 'revenger', 'simplifier'))
attack = sum(c[r] for r in ('reviewer', 'critic', 'mutation-tester'))
assert 32 <= n <= 64 and flash * 2 >= n and attack * 4 >= n, (n, flash, attack)
spec = {'wave': 'souji-r33-w1', 'reportDir': '.ufo/waves/round-33/w1', 'maxLanes': 64, 'context': CONTEXT, 'items': ITEMS}
json.dump(spec, open(L + '/.ufo/waves/round-33/w1-spec.json', 'w'), ensure_ascii=False, indent=1)
print(n, dict(c), 'flash', flash, 'attack', attack)
